id: pm-tnud
title: "Consolidate package lifecycle: extension/package/install/upgrade under a single pm package namespace"
description: "extension and package (already partial synonyms) plus top-level install and upgrade unify under pm package <verb> (install/upgrade/list/describe/enable/disable/...); extension, install, upgrade become hidden aliases. Duplicate check: pm-jqd2/pm-3wsi/pm-b3e9 are install-behavior bugs/hints, not surface consolidation."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:extensions",simplification
created_at: "2026-07-05T04:53:32.408Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-27T06:47:21.793Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-27T06:47:21.185Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-27T06:47:21.185Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: pm package covers the full extension/install/upgrade verb set with flag parity; extension/install/upgrade spellings alias-shimmed with identical output; scope semantics (project/global) unchanged; contracts/MCP/completions/docs regenerated; existing extension+install+upgrade specs pass via aliases
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Implemented
expected_result: "Package lifecycle is canonical under pm package, legacy extension/install/upgrade spellings remain hidden executable aliases with one suppressible hint, and CLI/SDK/contracts/completions/docs remain aligned."
actual_result: "pm package now owns lifecycle and upgrade discovery; hidden aliases preserve canonical stdout and emit config-aware migration hints; grammar, refusal recovery, generated surfaces, changelog scripts, and manual installed-package behavior are aligned."
